md='''# Batch102 independent QA\n\nExact source: `df19360a8d19068395f93c9da394c371f2ffb91d`.\n\n## Result\n\n- Arborea r003: STATIC_FIVE_STAGE_PASS.\n- Swartpuntia r002: STATIC_FIVE_STAGE_PASS.\n- Coronacollina r001: STATIC_FIVE_STAGE_PASS, with the original explicit2012 plate-availability limitation retained.\n- Echmatocrinus r002: STATIC_FIVE_STAGE_PASS.\n\nNo minimum geometry repair is required. Technical, visual, factual, specification and runtime_parse independently pass for these exact frozen subjects only. GPU and scene remain UNKNOWN; full seven-stage approved_for_brief remains false. This is not website/live/publication approval.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPersonally inspected32 separate final512 frames,4 lossless sheets,4 genuine concepts and3 exact-subject details, plus actual primary specimen pixels and primary text. All290 committed delivery paths, original complete freeze and dependency closure match. Both retained real generator rebuilds per model have distinct PIDs, valid queue chronology, unchanged pinned inputs and byte/semantic-identical GLBs.\n\nAn independent original-index binary audit finds356 closed consistently outward solids, without normal repair. Fresh transformed-source inspection establishes352 strict interior solid contacts, dense all-scene visibility diagnostics and actual frozen dimensions. All four complete source-collection reexports equal the shipped GLB bytes. Khronos reports0 errors/0 warnings, and all four parse with the pinned Three.js loader.\n\nArborea has64 attached pods with five real unit crests each; final detail resolves restrained modulation. Swartpuntia has3 oriented vanes and60 modules each, exposed on both sides with42 small axial nodes and no external stalk. Coronacollina has a measured18mm-wide/10mm-high cone, three rim peaks,1.8mm recess and four straight70/76/82/93mm spicules of0.7mm diameter. Echmatocrinus has8 unbranched arms,6 projections per arm,132 integral shallow plate cells and genuine basal overlap, not tangency.\n\n## Scientific scope\n\nThe2019 Arborea complete specimen has a short stem; the longer model stem is the explicit original genus-level artistic choice, not misattributed specimen anatomy. The2024 Swartpuntia restudy prospectively corrects historical stalk planning. Coronacollina's actual2015 holotype photo is distinct from its reconstruction panel; four spicules are selected, not universal, and no2012 plate inspection is claimed. Echmatocrinus affinity and mouth location remain uncertain; thin plate relief is not rigid crinoid armor, and185mm is not applied as an individual scale.\n\n## Preserved diagnostic correction\n\nThe initial independent reexport selected only the mesh and omitted the asset-root EMPTY, producing different node structure. This was a checker selection error, not an asset failure. Both initial outputs and corrected whole-collection reexports are retained; no original model was repaired.\n\nSee `independent-report.json` for exact subject/source/GLB/brief/reference hashes, `individual-frame-inspection.json` for each pixel judgment, `primary-source-inspection.json` for named sources and limitations, and `integrity-provenance.json` for hashes and actual rebuild evidence.\n'''
